			<div class="content" id="post-content-4789452">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Horror, History, Mystery</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout (Optional):</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Anomaly Classification System</li>
<li>Description</li>
<li>Documentation Analysis</li>
<li>Capture</li>
<li>Interview Logs</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;Pitch</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Ptich</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>A humanoid figure looking like a man from the middle east in his 30's.<br />
The Foundation has uncovered various texts, paintings, even videos depicting this figure next to rising political figures (Caesar, Ronald Reagan. Ivan the Terrible, Kim Il-Sung etc.).<br />
The Foundation decides to contain this SCP out of concern that it has malicious intentions in assisting these politicians. .</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;Narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Narrative</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Upon locating the SPC within a town in the Tigris–Euphrates river system, the foundation dispatches a Mobile Task Force which is subsequently killed (no survivors) by the inhabitants of the town.<br />
After a second MTF meets a similar fate (one survivor sent back with a message) the foundation dispatches one Field Agent with an ultimatum:<br />
&quot;Either the SCP surrenders to containment or the town will become a victim of a terrorist groups nuclear test&quot;.<br />
Following that the SCP has been moved to a containment site where it is most cooperative.<br />
The SCP seems to be interested in the inner workings of the foundation and its hierarchy.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;Hook</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Hook</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>The mystery of the SCP's end goal. It seems to be promoting certain people over others which does not always seem to be for the benefit of humanity.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong></p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Show&nbsp;Notes</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">-&nbsp;Hide&nbsp;Notes</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Upon containment the following anomalous properties have been discovered:</p>
<p>1. <strong>Psychic Influence - Friendly Face</strong>: Immediately upon contact with a subject the SCP's features alter so that they seem the most pleasing for that subject. Note: The effect works on an individual level, with every subject describing the end result differently. This effect works within a proximity 20 ft. and does not transmit through surveillance.<br />
2. ** Longevity/ Immortality <strong>: Upon questioning the SCP claims to be about 10000 years old, predating most known civilizations.<br />
3 **Regeneration</strong> - The SCP appears to be quickly regenerate from most wounds, even lethal.</p>
<p>Addendum:<br />
Upon questioning the SCP appears to have disdain, even hatred towards religion and deities.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

