			<div class="content" id="post-content-4789497">
									

<p>Interesting idea.</p>
<p>Right off the bat, I'd say you should change this &quot;King&quot; to a Political Advisor. If he is a king who wants to rule all of humanity, then why hasn't he yet? (Especially if he has mind controlling powers but we'll get to that later.) If he has helped put various political figures in positions of powers all throughout history, so they all in one form or another contribute to some big plan of his, it'll make much more sense to have him be a Political Advisor then because that's EXACTLY what many Political Advisors and other politicians have done throughout history.</p>
<p>Second, I fail to see how the mind control thing is necessary. If any human can do whatever he tells them too, then a) why hasn't he taken over the world? and b) how'd he get captured by the foundation and why hasn't he escaped from it? I mean I'm sure you can answer both questions, it's just you haven't made either clear as of yet. I wouldn't recommend though having him to decide to stay with the foundation because that's also part of his larger plan, because that's already basically the plot of SCP-343.</p>
<p>This is an interesting scenario, because for most ideas, they can really only go one direction or multiple. But in this case I can only really see two directions you can take this to. 1: You make him a Moriarty-like immortal human who wants to take over the world, as is playing a very careful game of chess with the politicians of the world and throughout to accomplish that (you should add a few more anomolaous traits if you choose this one.) 2: There are various god and god-like entities in the SCP universe. Based on my knowledge, roughly 99% hates humanity and/or wants to destroy humanity (or just doesn't even waste time with dealing in humanity). Maybe make this &quot;Kingmaker,&quot; a god of humanity who genuinely wants to protect it from those other forces, but does so via mind control and complete obedience to him. Out of those two, I'd recommend the first one because it is both easier and more fun. Good luck!</p>

							</div>

								
