<p>The problem with having a big idea and Winrar in your brain rather than zip.</p>
<p>1. Why hasn't he taken over yet?<br />
He's not malicious. At least not according to him. He wants to become King of all again, but not by force. So his big plan is to make life not under his rule so terrible, that people will let him.</p>
<p>2. The Mind control.<br />
The mind control is something I envisioned him having to place his as Keter or Euclid.<br />
On how f-ed up his power is: &quot;Jerry get out of the booth, take your clothes off and fold yourself twelve times&quot;. Basically that scene from Rick and Morty. As he would explain it: &quot;Humanity promised me its obedience. I expect it. &quot;</p>
<p>3. On how he got captured?<br />
He has established a small community (around 1000 people) in the middle-east that have accepted him as their ruler. The foundation is threatening them. As a generous and benevolent leader he agreed to comply with the foundations demands.</p>
<p>4. Why he remains?<br />
The current leaders of the foundation are the ones who threaten his subjects. He has made many new leaders rise to power. All he needs is time.</p>
<p>5. On the god angle.<br />
So far I came up that he HATES dieties. Especially the judeo-christian one (so will be fun if he finds out about 343.). The reason would be that God is the reason that his kingdom no longer exists. According to him. Tower of Babel story.</p>

